\subsection{Staged with Role Instructions}
\label{app:staged-roles}
The \condStagedRoles\ condition was added after the main results had been observed, to test whether the role instructions of our subagents explain the advantage over \condStaged.
It reuses the \condStaged\ harness, stage order, and trace format, and adds to the \texttt{Pre-Write}, \texttt{Write}, and \texttt{Re-Write} prompts the \texttt{Planner}, \texttt{Translator}, and \texttt{Reviewer} role instructions, without the text that refers to the \texttt{Monitor}, goals, trace, shared files, or delegation.
It was generated once on generation run 1 and judged with the run-1 pairwise setup, so the \condAgenticCogWriter\ comparison covers the \FullStagedRolesAcrossN\ prompts with a completed run-1 output.
Table~\ref{tab:appendix-staged-roles} reports both contrasts: our system is preferred on WritingBench and HelloBench but not significantly on DoLoMiTes, and \condStagedRoles\ loses to \condStaged\ on HelloBench and is near parity elsewhere.
