\subsection{Cross-Family Judge Robustness}
\label{app:cross-family}
Table~\ref{tab:appendix-cross-family} reports benchmark-level results for the five cross-family contrasts between our system and an alternative or ablation, all on generation run 1.
Within each contrast, summing W/L/T counts over the three benchmarks gives \CrossFamilyFullSinglePassWLT\ versus \condSinglePass, \CrossFamilyFullStagedWLT\ versus \condStaged, \CrossFamilyFullTaskPlanningWLT\ versus \condTaskPlanning, \CrossFamilyFullNoGoalsWLT\ versus \condNoGoals, and \CrossFamilyFullFixedOrderWLT\ versus \condFixedOrder.
The corresponding Wilson intervals are \CrossFamilyFullSinglePassInterval, \CrossFamilyFullStagedInterval, \CrossFamilyFullTaskPlanningInterval, \CrossFamilyFullNoGoalsInterval, and \CrossFamilyFullFixedOrderInterval, with sign-test $p=\CrossFamilyFullStagedP$ against \condStaged\ and $p=\CrossFamilyFullFixedOrderP$ against \condFixedOrder.
The \condStaged\ and \condFixedOrder\ contrasts cover \CrossFamilyFullStagedN\ and \CrossFamilyFullFixedOrderN\ pairs; one further pair, a HelloBench comparison with \condStaged, failed the judge's structured-output check after all retries and has no cross-family outcome.
Across all five contrasts and benchmarks, the judge yields a non-tied order-consistent outcome on \CrossFamilyPooledCommitRate\ of \CrossFamilyPooledN\ eligible pairs, with \CrossFamilyPooledWLT\ W/L/T; \CrossFamilyPooledAgreement\ prompt-level outcomes agree with the same-family judge.
Cohen's kappa between the two judges is \JudgeAgreementKappa\ over these outcomes, most of which are cross-family ties, and \JudgeAgreementDecidedKappa\ over the \JudgeAgreementDecidedPairs\ pairs both judges decide, of which \JudgeAgreementDecidedAgreeing\ agree.

